    "answer": {
      "short": "$192$ codes.\n\nAdd the cases with zero, one and two Os, dividing by $2!$ when both Os are used.",
      "worked": "The four distinct non-O letters are M, N, I and D.\n\nNo O: $\\binom{4}{4}4!=24$.\n\nOne O: $\\binom{4}{3}4!=96$.\n\nTwo Os: $\\binom{4}{2}\\dfrac{4!}{2!}=72$. Divide by $2!$ because the Os are identical.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\binom{4}{4}4!+\\binom{4}{3}4!+\\binom{4}{2}\\frac{4!}{2!}\\\\N&=24+96+72\\\\N&=192\\end{align*}$$\nThere are $192$ codes.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 36
  },
